00:00:03.510 --> 00:00:06.230 align:start position:0%
after weeks of speculation philippine  president rodrigo duterte has through a  representative filed his candidacy for  senator  the move comes after he publicly rebuked  his own daughter davao city mayor sarah  duterte for running as vice president  and running mate of the son of the late  dictator ferdinand marcus ferdinand  marcus jr  the older duterte says his daughter is  far more popular than marcus and that  the marcuses can never be trusted  especially when it comes to politics  that's a surprise to many because the  marcuses have been allies of the  dutertes since 2016.  for months now the dutertes have  repeatedly said they were not interested  in seeking higher office that's changed  in the past couple of days  so you can see how  they treat philippine politics it's like  a game and you know what shows also is  their very strong sense of entitlement  we've seen how the substitution works  we've seen how  personalities or people we do not know  filed candidacies for president vice  president senator only to withdraw and  then only to be place holders and give  way to personalities  while this may seem a typical jostle for  political power it is critical for  duterte's administration to remain in  control beyond 2022 president duterte is  facing investigations before the  criminal court for crimes against  humanity in his so-called war on drugs  which has left thousands of filipinos  dead  he and his allies are also expected to  face multiple cases for alleged  involvement in several corruption  scandals  critics say the administration may be  preoccupied with its own political  survival but much more is at stake for  the rest of the country next year  the next administration will inherit  unprecedented challenges the country is  still reeling from the impact of the  corona pandemic there is an ever  increasing national debt and growing  military tensions in the south china sea  even for a country with a long history  of upheaval during elections this is  unprecedented the 2022 elections will  not just be a battle between opposing  political parties but a fight between  powerful political dynasties jamal  alindogan al jazeera manila
 

